      "value": "The hypothesis posits that apparent rigidity in N_c(w) is an optimization artifact. The previous prediction (surprise=0.96) likely failed because the solver got trapped in local minima at low widths. To verify, I will first perform a bootstrap feasibility check (Step 0) to ensure zero-violation is reachable with the proposed L-BFGS-B optimizer and sufficient capacity. If reachable, I will run a systematic width scan (h=1 to h_max=50) across multiple constraint widths (w) and random seeds, using multi-start optimization to avoid local traps. This will produce the N_c(w) table and trend analysis needed to distinguish between true rigidity (flat/decreasing N_c) and optimization failure (increasing N_c or false flatness)."
