      "value": "If the hypothesis were that 'N_c should be flat or decreasing as width increases for linear constraints,' this output directly contradicts it by showing a strict linear increase (~0.58 per unit width). The system would crash by misinterpreting growing N_c as evidence of non-rigidity when it may simply reflect additive boundary effects in a rigid system."
